Finished? YES
Shipped in 0.10.1 as **VACUUM**. Every 10,000 points the arena empties itself into the ship for ten
seconds: every shard in the world and not only the ones on screen (the window is a tenth of the arena,
and the loot you never saw is the loot you would swear was there), and anything you kill during those
ten seconds comes in the moment it drops. The fanfare is the music's business, as you asked of music:
the run keeps its tempo, its drums and its chord, and for the ten seconds the little arpeggio is spent
on a rising tune in the same key - so it plays *over* the fight you were in, boss music and all, and
stops when the well closes. A gold `VACUUM` and a countdown appear by the score, and a ring opens wide
round the ship and collapses in to say how much floor was coming.

Measured, because free shards are free levels: ten runs either side of it read +13.9% score, +16.5%
levels and +49.5% shards at the median - about half of what a card you pay a level for is worth, which
is what keeps it a reward and not a second build to optimise. The first one lands about 2m30s into a
good run, then one every minute or two.

No screen shake and no freeze in it, on purpose: your "only shake extraordinarily" rule still holds,
and a freeze between a pause and its resume turns a press into a dash you never asked for.
